---
title: Propose a course
description: The three-step form where you describe your course, lesson by lesson, until you send it for review.
sidebar:
  order: 5
---

The form has **three steps** and you can move freely between them. Required fields aren't validated until you press **Submit course**, so you can fill it in whatever order you like.

Open it with **Create course** from your instructor space.

{% aside title="It saves itself" %}
Autosave is on. Close the tab whenever you want and pick it up later from [My courses](/en/profesores/mis-cursos/).
{% /aside %}

## Step 1 · Course details

- **Course name**
- **Course type**:
  - **MOOC (self-paced)** — the student moves at their own speed.
  - **Cohort-based (with a calendar)** — a group moves together on fixed dates.
- **Course language**
- **Start date** and **end date**
- **Number of lessons**
- **Recurrence**, **schedule** and **time zone**

Recurrence and schedule are what make a cohort course work; in a MOOC they mostly signal a suggested pace.

## Step 2 · About the course

This is the case for why your course should exist:

- **Elevator pitch**
- **What problem it solves** for students
- **3 learning objectives**
- **Your ideal student**
- **Introduction video (optional):** 1 to 2 minutes, shared through an **unlisted** YouTube link. See the [recording and sharing guide](/en/profesores/video-presentacion/) and [script template](/en/profesores/video-presentacion/#script-template).
- The **rights** checkbox: *"I hold the rights to the content and agree to share it under an open licence"*

{% aside type="caution" title="Open licence" %}
Ticking that box isn't a formality. It means the material is published under an open licence, so don't include third-party content you don't hold the rights to.
{% /aside %}

## Step 3 · Content per lesson

You add lessons one at a time with **Add lesson**. For each one you describe:

- **Lesson title**
- **Topics** — added one by one
- **Objectives**
- **Activities**
- **Materials** — links with **Add link**, or files with **Attach file**

Every item has its own **Remove** in case you added one too many.

## Submitting

Before the **Submit course** button works, these have to be sorted:

- A complete [instructor profile](/en/profesores/perfil/) — if something's missing you'll see **Complete profile →**.
- [GitHub connected](/en/profesores/github/) — if not, **Connect GitHub →**.
- The form's required fields. If any are missing you'll see *"Required fields are missing or there are errors. Check the marked fields."*

On submission we create your course's space on GitHub and open a **Pull Request**. You'll see *"Opening Pull Request…"* and, once it's ready, the link and the next steps.

## What happens next

Your proposal is reviewed in that GitHub Pull Request: that's where you'll get the feedback and where it gets approved. You can follow its status in [My courses](/en/profesores/mis-cursos/).
